---Describes a GraphQL API.
---@class aws.appsync.GraphqlApi
---@field name? aws.appsync.ResourceName The API name.
---@field apiId? aws.appsync.String The API ID.
---@field authenticationType? aws.appsync.AuthenticationType The authentication type.
---@field logConfig? aws.appsync.LogConfig The Amazon CloudWatch Logs configuration.
---@field userPoolConfig? aws.appsync.UserPoolConfig The Amazon Cognito user pool configuration.
---@field openIDConnectConfig? aws.appsync.OpenIDConnectConfig The OpenID Connect configuration.
---@field arn? aws.appsync.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN).
---@field uris? aws.appsync.MapOfStringToString The URIs.
---@field tags? aws.appsync.TagMap The tags.
---@field additionalAuthenticationProviders? aws.appsync.AdditionalAuthenticationProviders A list of additional authentication providers for the GraphqlApi API.
---@field xrayEnabled aws.appsync.Boolean A flag indicating whether to use X-Ray tracing for this GraphqlApi.
---@field wafWebAclArn? aws.appsync.String The ARN of the WAF access control list (ACL) associated with this GraphqlApi, if one exists.
---@field lambdaAuthorizerConfig? aws.appsync.LambdaAuthorizerConfig Configuration for Lambda function authorization.
---@field dns? aws.appsync.MapOfStringToString The DNS records for the API.
---@field visibility? aws.appsync.GraphQLApiVisibility Sets the value of the GraphQL API to public (GLOBAL) or private (PRIVATE). If no value is provided, the visibility will be set to GLOBAL by default. This value cannot be changed once the API has been created.
---@field apiType? aws.appsync.GraphQLApiType The value that indicates whether the GraphQL API is a standard API (GRAPHQL) or merged API (MERGED).
---@field mergedApiExecutionRoleArn? aws.appsync.String The Identity and Access Management service role ARN for a merged API. The AppSync service assumes this role on behalf of the Merged API to validate access to source APIs at runtime and to prompt the AUTO_MERGE to update the merged API endpoint with the source API changes automatically.
---@field owner? aws.appsync.String The account owner of the GraphQL API.
---@field ownerContact? aws.appsync.String The owner contact information for an API resource.
---@field introspectionConfig? aws.appsync.GraphQLApiIntrospectionConfig Sets the value of the GraphQL API to enable (ENABLED) or disable (DISABLED) introspection. If no value is provided, the introspection configuration will be set to ENABLED by default. This field will produce an error if the operation attempts to use the introspection feature while this field is disabled.
---@field queryDepthLimit aws.appsync.QueryDepthLimit The maximum depth a query can have in a single request. Depth refers to the amount of nested levels allowed in the body of query. The default value is 0 (or unspecified), which indicates there's no depth limit. If you set a limit, it can be between 1 and 75 nested levels. This field will produce a limit error if the operation falls out of bounds.
---@field resolverCountLimit aws.appsync.ResolverCountLimit The maximum number of resolvers that can be invoked in a single request. The default value is 0 (or unspecified), which will set the limit to 10000. When specified, the limit value can be between 1 and 10000. This field will produce a limit error if the operation falls out of bounds.
---@field enhancedMetricsConfig? aws.appsync.EnhancedMetricsConfig The enhancedMetricsConfig object.

